essive documentation and context-aware development workflows"},"features":{"zh":["PRD驱动的上下文工程","AI智能产品的快速开发","提高生产力和效率","支持Next.js和Supabase","提供模板和工作流"],"ja":["PRD駆動のコンテキストエンジニアリング","AIエージェントの迅速開発","生産性と効率の向上","Next.jsとSupabaseのサポート","テンプレートとワークフローの提供"],"ko":["PRD 주도적 컨텍스트 엔지니어링","AI 에이전트의 신속 개발","생산성과 효율性的 향상","Next.js와 Supabase의 지원","템플릿과 워크플로우의 제공"],"es":["Desarrollo de productos con documentación progresiva","Flujos de trabajo de desarrollo de contexto","Integración con Next.js y Supabase","Plantillas para desarrollo rápido","Herramientas de productividad para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Développement de produits avec documentation progressive","Flux de travail de développement de contexte","Intégration avec Next.js et Supabase","Modèles pour développement rapide","Outils de productivité pour développeurs"],"de":["Produktentwicklung mit fortschreitender Dokumentation","Kontext-Entwicklungs-Workflows","Integration mit Next.js und Supabase","Vorlagen für schnelles Entwickeln","Produktivitäts-Tools für Entwickler"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de produtos de IA com documentação progressiva","Fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento sensíveis ao contexto","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento de IA como NextJS e Supabase","Melhoria da produtividade com templates e workflows personalizados","Suporte a desenvolvedores com ferramentas de CLI e React"],"ru":["Разработка продуктов ИИ с прогрессивной документацией","Контекстно-зависимые рабочие процессы разработки","Интеграция с инструментами разработки ИИ như NextJS и Supabase","Повышение производительности с помощью шаблонов и рабочих процессов","Поддержка разработчиков с помощью инструментов CLI и React"],"ar":["تطوير منتجات الذكاء الاصطناعي مع توثيق متقدم","عمليات عمل مطورة حساسة للسياق","التكامل مع أدوات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل NextJS و Supabase","تحسين الإنتاجية مع قوالب وعمليات عمل مخصصة","دعم المطورين بأدوات CLI و React"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具","PRD驱动的上下文工程","快速开发","生产力和效率","Next.js","Supabase","模板和工作流","如何使用prd-v03-moat-definition","prd-v03-moat-definition安装指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","PRD駆動のコンテキストエンジニアリング","迅速開発","生産性と効率","Next.js","Supabase","テンプレートとワークフロー","prd-v03-moat-definitionの使い方","prd-v03-moat-definitionの設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","PRD 주도적 컨텍스트 엔지니어링","신속 개발","생산성과 효율性","Next.js","Supabase","템플릿과 워크플로우","prd-v03-moat-definition의 사용법","prd-v03-moat-definition의 설정 가이드"],"es":["cómo utilizar herramientas de agente de inteligencia artificial","qué es la ingeniería de contexto","prd-v03-moat-definition alternativa","prd-v03-moat-definition vs herramientas de desarrollo","instalación de prd-v03-moat-definition","guía de configuración de prd-v03-moat-definition","herramientas de desarrollo de inteligencia artificial","desarrollo de productos con inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["comment utiliser les outils d''agents d''intelligence artificielle","quoi est l''ingénierie de contexte","prd-v03-moat-definition alternative","prd-v03-moat-definition vs outils de développement","installation de prd-v03-moat-definition","guide de configuration de prd-v03-moat-definition","outils de développement d''intelligence artificielle","développement de produits avec intelligence artificielle"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten-Tools verwendet","was ist Kontext-Engineerung","prd-v03-moat-definition Alternative","prd-v03-moat-definition vs Entwicklungs-Tools","Installation von prd-v03-moat-definition","Einrichtungs-Anleitung für prd-v03-moat-definition","KI-Entwicklungs-Tools","Produktentwicklung mit KI"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de IA","o que é PRD-driven Context Engineering","ferramentas de desenvolvimento de IA","alternativas ao NextJS","Supabase vs Firebase","guia de instalação do React","configuração do CLI para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать инструменты ИИ","что такое PRD-driven Context Engineering","инструменты разработки ИИ","альтернативы NextJS","Supabase vs Firebase","руководство по установке React","настройка CLI для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هي هندسة السياق القائمة على وثائق المتطلبات","أدوات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديلات ل NextJS","Supabase مقابل Firebase","دليل تثبيت React","ضبط CLI للمطورين"]}},"owner":"mattgierhart","repo":"PRD-driven-context-engineering","repoPath":"mattgierhart/PRD-driven-context-engineering","stars":24,"forks":4,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T18:03:27Z","topics":["ai-assisted","claude","developer-tools","nextjs","product-development","productivity","rapid-development","supabase","templates","workflow"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prd-v03-moat-definition","description":"Assess competitor defensibility and define our own moat strategy during PRD v0.3 Commercial Model. Triggers on requests to analyze competitor moats, define our defensibility, assess switching costs, identify vulnerabilities, find wedge opportunities, or when user asks whats our moat?, how defensible are they?, where can we compete?, switching costs?, defensibility, who to target. Consumes Competitive Landscape (v0.2) CFD- entries. Outputs CFD- entries for competitor moats and BR- entries for targeting rules and our defensibility strategy.","bodyPreview":"# Moat Definition\n\nPosition in HORIZON workflow: v0.2 Competitive Landscape → **v0.3 Moat Definition** → v0.3 Pricing Model Selection\n\n## Consumes\n\nThis skill requires prior work from v0.2:\n\n- **Landscape map artifact** (from Competitive Landscape Mapping) — Current behavior documentation, feature matrix, competitor analysis\n- **CFD-\\* entries** (competitive intelligence, from Competitive Landscape Mapping) — Documented competitors with pricing, features, user feedback\n- **BR-\\* product type ent","body":"# Moat Definition\n\nPosition in HORIZON workflow: v0.2 Competitive Landscape → **v0.3 Moat Definition** → v0.3 Pricing Model Selection\n\n## Consumes\n\nThis skill requires prior work from v0.2:\n\n- **Landscape map artifact** (from Competitive Landscape Mapping) — Current behavior documentation, feature matrix, competitor analysis\n- **CFD-\\* entries** (competitive intelligence, from Competitive Landscape Mapping) — Documented competitors with pricing, features, user feedback\n- **BR-\\* product type entry** (from Product Type Classification) — Classification constrains which competitors are relevant to analyze\n\nThis skill assumes v0.2 analysis is complete with documented competitors.\n\n## Produces\n\nThis skill creates/updates:\n\n- **CFD-\\* entries** (competitor moat analysis) — Assessment of each competitor''s defensibility by moat type\n- **BR-\\* entries** (targeting rules) — Constraints derived from moat analysis, defining where to compete vs. avoid\n- **Moat strength inventory artifact** — Summary of competitor moats with vulnerability signals\n\nAll CFD moat analysis entries should include:\n- `confidence: 2-3/5` (based on public evidence + user interviews about switching friction)\n- Evidence source (pricing pages, reviews, customer interviews)\n- Forward target: \"Would move to 4/5 if we interview 5+ current/former customers about switching costs\"\n\nExample moat analysis entry:\n```markdown\nCFD-055: Competitor Moat Analysis — Notion\n\nCompetitor: Notion\nPrimary Moat Type: Switching Costs (data lock-in)\nMoat Strength Tier: Strong\nConfidence: 3/5 (source: public-research + 2-user-interviews)\nDate: 2026-02-01\n\nSwitching Cost Quantification:\n  - Financial: Multi-year contract, no early termination ($0 direct cost)\n  - Time/Effort: 20+ hours migration, team retraining\n  - Data Migration: Proprietary database format (complex export)\n  - Workflow Retraining: Unique templates, team habits\n  - Integration Rework: Deep Slack/GitHub dependencies\n\nTotal Switching Cost: $3K in labor + 20 hours = Material friction\nMoat Verdict: Strong — switching costs >$3K + meaningful time investment\n\nVulnerability Signal: SMB segment with small teams; they use <20% of feature set (opportunity for simpler tool)\nTargeting Decision: Avoid direct competition. Wedge in SMB with simplified, cheaper offering.\n\nEvidence:\n  - CFD-042 (landscape): Reviews show enterprise love; SMB complaints focus on cost + complexity\n  - CFD-015 (value hypothesis): SMB would save $12,500/year with simpler tool\nNext Target: \"Would move to 4/5 if we interview 5+ SMB teams about exact switching cost dollars\"\n```\n\n## Moat Type Taxonomy\n\nEvery moat falls into one of six types. Identify primary + secondary moats per competitor:\n\n| Moat Type | Definition | Strong When | Weak When |\n|-----------|------------|-------------|-----------|\n| **Switching Costs** | Friction to leave (data, workflow, contracts) | Multi-year data, deep integrations | Easy export, monthly contracts |\n| **Network Effects** | Value increases with users | Two-sided marketplace, content platform | Single-player tool, linear value |\n| **Data/IP** | Proprietary data or algorithms | Unique training data, patents | Commodity ML, public datasets |\n| **Brand/Trust** | Recognition, credibility | Regulated industry, high-risk decisions | Low-stakes, undifferentiated |\n| **Scale/Cost** | Volume economics | Infrastructure-heavy, marginal cost near zero | Labor-intensive, linear cost |\n| **Regulatory** | Compliance barriers | Certifications required, government contracts | No compliance requirements |\n\n**For micro-SaaS**: Switching costs and brand/trust matter most. Network effects and scale rarely apply.\n\n## Moat Strength Tiers\n\nRate each competitor''s defensibility:\n\n| Tier | Criteria | Evidence Signals | Targeting Implication |\n|------|----------|------------------|----------------------|\n| **Impenetrable** | Multi-layered moat, 10+ years data lock-in | \"Would take years to switch\" | Avoid direct competition |\n| **Strong** | Significant switching friction, 1-2 year contracts | High NPS + low churn despite complaints | Target underserved segments only |\n| **Moderate** | Some friction, workarounds exist | Churn 5-10%, export options | Wedge opportunity exists |\n| **Weak** | Easy to replace, commodity offering | Monthly plans, high churn, price shopping | Direct competition viable |\n| **Eroding** | Former strength declining | New alternatives gaining share | Aggressive targeting |\n\n**Gate rule**: Don''t compete where incumbent has Impenetrable or Strong moat unless targeting segment they explicitly ignore.\n\n## Switching Cost Inventory\n\nQuantify ALL switching costs — the sum determines moat strength:\n\n| Cost Type | High Impact | Low Impact | How to Assess |\n|-----------|-------------|------------|---------------|\n| **Financial** | >6mo contract, early termination fees | Monthly billing, no penalty | Check pricing page terms |\n| **Time/Effort** | 40+ hr migration, retraining | <4 hr setup, familiar UX | Trial the competitor |\n| **Data Migration** | Proprietary format, no export | Standard export (CSV, API) | Test export function |\n| **Workflow Retraining** | Unique methodology, team habits | Standard patterns | Read onboarding docs |\n| **Integration Rework** | Deep API dependencies | Standalone tool | Map their integrations |\n\n**Calculation**: Sum hours + dollars. >$5K or >40hr = material switching cost.\n\n## Targeting Decision Framework\n\nUse moat analysis to determine where to compete:\n\n```\nMoat Impenetrable/Strong → DON''T COMPETE HERE\n                          ↓ unless\n                          Target ignored segment (SMB, specific vertical)\n                          \nMoat Moderate → WEDGE STRATEGY\n                ↓ identify\n                Entry point that bypasses switching friction\n                \nMoat Weak/Eroding → DIRECT COMPETITION\n                    ↓ execute\n                    Feature + price attack on their core\n```\n\n### Wedge Opportunity Signals\n\nA wedge exists when:\n- Competitor moat doesn''t apply to specific segment\n- One feature has LOW switching cost (can start there)\n- Integration allows coexistence (not replacement)\n- Price sensitivity > switching friction\n\n## Analysis Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Pull Competitor Data\nRetrieve CFD- entries from v0.2 Competitive Landscape. For each competitor, you need: pricing, complaints, feature set.\n\n### Step 2: Identify Moat Type\nFor each competitor, determine primary moat type. Use evidence from reviews, pricing structure, integration depth.\n\n### Step 3: Rate Moat Strength\nApply tier criteria. Flag if insufficient evidence (Tier 4-5 confidence).\n\n### Step 4: Inventory Switching Costs\nComplete the 5-category switching cost assessment. Quantify hours + dollars.\n\n### Step 5: Identify Vulnerabilities\nWhere is their moat weakest? Which segments do they ignore? What''s eroding?\n\n### Step 6: Generate IDs\n\n**CFD entries** (customer_feedback.md):\nTemplate: [assets/cfd-moat-analysis.md](assets/cfd-moat-analysis.md)\n```\nCFD-MOT-###: [Competitor] Moat Analysis — [Moat Type], [Strength Tier]\n```\n\n**BR entries** (BUSINESS_RULES.md):\nTemplate: [assets/br-targeting.md](assets/br-targeting.md)\n```\nBR-TGT-###: [Targeting Rule] — based on [Competitor] moat weakness\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n| Don''t | Do Instead |\n|-------|------------|\n| \"They''re big\" | Specify which moat type + evidence |\n| Assume low switching cost | Quantify: hours + dollars |\n| Only analyze direct competitors | Include Type 4-5 (workarounds, inertia) |\n| Underestimate integration moat | Map actual dependency depth |\n| Ignore eroding moats | Track signals: new entrants, complaints |\n| Target where moat is strong | Find the segment where moat doesn''t apply |\n\n## Output Requirements\n\nBefore advancing to Our Moat Articulation:\n- [ ] ≥3 competitors with moat type identified\n- [ ] ≥2 competitors with switching costs quantified\n- [ ] Moat strength tier assigned (with evidence)\n- [ ] Targeting decision per competitor (compete/avoid/wedge)\n- [ ] CFD-MOT entries created (≥3)\n- [ ] BR-TGT entries created (≥2)\n\n## Downstream Connections\n\n| Consumer | What It Needs | Format |\n|----------|---------------|--------|\n| **v0.3 Our Moat Articulation** | Where competitors are weak, what moats work | CFD-MOT entries |\n| **v0.3 Pricing Model** | What price points bypass switching friction | BR-TGT entries |\n| **v0.5 Red Team** | Risks of competitor response | Moat strength tiers |\n| **v0.9 GTM** | Positioning against competitor moats | Targeting rules |\n\n## Detailed References\n\n- **Good/bad examples**: See `references/examples.md`\n- **CFD-MOT template**: See `assets/cfd-moat-analysis.md`\n- **BR-TGT template**: See `assets/br-targeting.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T07:39:58.738Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Product Development Agents needing systematic approaches to building AI-powered products with context-aware development workflows","zh":"非常适合需要系统方法来构建具有上下文感知开发工作流的AI驱动产品的产品开发代理","ja":"AIを活用した製品を構築するための体系的なアプローチが必要な製品開発エージェントに最適","ko":"시스템적인 접근 방식으로 Context-Aware 개발 워크플ロー와 함께 AI 기반 제품을 구축해야 하는 제품 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de Productos que necesitan enfoques sistemáticos para crear productos con tecnología de inteligencia artificial y flujos de trabajo de desarrollo con conciencia de contexto","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement de Produits ayant besoin d''approches systématiques pour créer des produits alimentés par l''IA avec des flux de travail de développement sensibles au contexte","de":"Perfekt für Produktentwicklungsagenten, die systematische Ansätze für die Erstellung von künstlicher Intelligenz-basierten Produkten mit kontextbewussten Entwicklungsworkflows benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Produto que precisam de abordagens sistemáticas para construir produtos impulsionados por IA com fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento cientes de contexto","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по разработке продуктов, которым необходимы системные подходы к созданию продуктов на основе ИИ с контекстно-зависимыми рабочими процессами разработки","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تطوير المنتجات الذين يحتاجون إلى نهج منهجي لإنشاء منتجات مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي مع تدفقات عمل تطوير معينة السياق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to engineer context-driven product development using progressive documentation, leveraging landscape maps and competitive intelligence to define a moat, and integrating with workflows like HORIZON for seamless product lifecycle management, utilizing artifacts like landscape map and CFD entries","zh":"赋予代理工程师使用进步文档、利用景观地图和竞争情报来定义护城河，并将工作流如HORIZON集成以实现无缝产品生命周期管理，利用景观地图和CFD条目等工件","ja":"文書化の進歩に従ったコンテキストドリブン製品開発をエージェントが実現できるようにし、競合情勢地図や競争情報を利用して護城河を定義し、HORIZONなどのワークフローと統合して製品ライフサイクル管理を円滑に実現し、景観地図やCFDエントリなどのアーティファクトを利用","ko":"에이전트가 프로그레시브 문서를 사용하여 컨텍스트 드리븐 제품 개발을 구축하고 경쟁 지형도 및 경쟁 정보를 사용하여护城河를 정의하며 HORIZON과 같은 워크플로와 통합하여 제품 수명주기 관리를 원활하게 수행하며 지형도 및 CFD 항목과 같은 아티팩트를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ingenierizar el desarrollo de productos impulsado por el contexto utilizando documentación progresiva, aprovechando mapas de paisaje y inteligencia competitiva para definir una trinchera, e integrándose con flujos de trabajo como HORIZON para una gestión del ciclo de vida del producto sin problemas, utilizando artefactos como mapas de paisaje y entradas de CFD","fr":"Permet aux agents d''ingénieriser le développement de produits impulsé par le contexte en utilisant une documentation progressive, en exploitant les cartes de paysage et le renseignement compétitif pour définir une tranchée, et en intégrant avec des flux de travail comme HORIZON pour une gestion du cycle de vie du produit sans heurts, en utilisant des artefacts tels que des cartes de paysage et des entrées CFD","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, kontextgetriebene Produktentwicklung zu konzipieren, indem progressive Dokumentation, Landschaftskarten und Wettbewerbsanalyse zur Definition einer Marktnische genutzt werden, und sich in Workflows wie HORIZON integrieren, um eine nahtlose Produktlebenszyklusverwaltung zu ermöglichen, unter Nutzung von Artefakten wie Landschaftskarten und CFD-Einträgen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar o desenvolvimento de produtos orientado por contexto, utilizando documentação progressiva, aproveitando mapas de paisagem e inteligência competitiva para definir um fosso, e integrando com fluxos de trabalho como o HORIZON para gerenciamento de ciclo de vida de produtos sem interrupções, utilizando artefatos como mapa de paisagem e entradas de CFD","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать контекстно-ориентированное развитие продукта, используя прогрессивную документацию, используя карты ландшафта и конкурентную разведку для определения рва, и интегрируя с рабочими процессами, такими как HORIZON, для бесшовного управления жизненным циклом продукта, используя артефакты, такие как карта ландшафта и записи CFD","ar":"يتمكّن الوكلاء من هندسة تطوير المنتجات القائمة على السياق باستخدام توثيق تقدمي، واستفادة من خرائط المناظر الطبيعية والاستخبارات التنافسية لتعريف خندق، ودمجها مع تدفقات العمل مثل HORIZON لإدارة دورة حياة المنتج دون انقطاع، باستخدام مكونات مثل خريطة المناظر الطبيعية ومشاركات CFD"},"useCases":{"en":["Defining a moat in a competitive landscape","Generating product development roadmaps with context-aware workflows","Integrating competitive intelligence into product development cycles"],"zh":["在竞争地形中定义护城河","使用上下文感知工作流生成产品开发路线图","将竞争情报集成到产品开发周期"],"ja":["競合地図の中でモートを定義する","コンテキストアウェアワークフローを使用して製品開発ロードマップを生成する","競争情報を製品開発サイクルに統合する"],"ko":["경쟁 지형에서護城河를 정의","컨텍스트 인식 워크플로를 사용하여 제품 개발 로드맵 생성","경쟁 정보를 제품 개발 주기에 통합"],"es":["Definir una trinchera en un paisaje competitivo","Generar hojas de ruta de desarrollo de productos con flujos de trabajo con conciencia de contexto","Integrar inteligencia competitiva en ciclos de desarrollo de productos"],"fr":["Définir une tranchée dans un paysage compétitif","Générer des feuilles de route de développement de produits avec des flux de travail sensibles au contexte","Intégrer le renseignement compétitif dans les cycles de développement de produits"],"de":["Definieren einer Marktnische in einem wettbewerbsorientierten Umfeld","Erstellen von Produktentwicklungs-Roadmaps mit kontextbewussten Workflows","Integrieren von Wettbewerbsanalyse in Produktentwicklungszyklen"],"pt":["Definir um fosso em uma paisagem competitiva","Gerar mapas de estrada de desenvolvimento de produtos com fluxos de trabalho cientes de contexto","Integrar inteligência competitiva em ciclos de desenvolvimento de produtos"],"ru":["Определение рва в конкурентной среде","Генерация дорожных карт разработки продукта с контекстно-зависимыми рабочими процессами","Интеграция конкурентной разведки в циклы разработки продукта"],"ar":["تحديد خندق في مناظر تنافسية","توليد خطط طريق لتطوير المنتجات مع تدفقات عمل معينة السياق","دمج الاستخبارات التنافسية في دورات تطوير المنتجات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires prior work from Competitive Landscape Mapping (v0.2)","Needs landscape map artifact and CFD entries","Specific to HORIZON workflow integration"],"zh":["需要竞争地形映射（v0.2）的先行工作","需要地图工件和CFD条目","特定于HORIZON工作流集成"],"ja":["競合地図マッピング（v0.2）の先行作業が必要","地図アーティファクトとCFDエントリが必要","HORIZONワークフロー統合に特有"],"ko":["경쟁 지형 매핑(v0.2)의 선행 작업 필요","지도 아티팩트 및 CFD 항목 필요","HORIZON 워크플로 통합에 특정"],"es":["Requiere trabajo previo de Mapeo de Paisaje Competitivo (v0.2)","Necesita artefacto de mapa de paisaje y entradas de CFD","Específico para la integración del flujo de trabajo HORIZON"],"fr":["Nécessite un travail préalable de Cartographie de Paysage Compétitif (v0.2)","Nécessite un artefact de carte de paysage et des entrées CFD","Spécifique à l''intégration du flux de travail HORIZON"],"de":["Benötigt vorherige Arbeit von Wettbewerbslandschaftsmapping (v0.2)","Benötigt Landschaftskarten-Artefakt und CFD-Einträge","Spezifisch für die Integration des HORIZON-Workflows"],"pt":["Exige trabalho prévio do Mapeamento de Paisagem Competitiva (v0.2)","Necessita de artefato de mapa de paisagem e entradas de CFD","Específico para integração do fluxo de trabalho HORIZON"],"ru":["Требует предварительной работы по картографированию конкурентной среды (v0.2)","Требует артефакта карты ландшафта и записей CFD","Спécífico для интеграции с рабочим процессом HORIZON"],"ar":["يتطلب عملًا سابقًا من خريطة المناظر الطبيعية التنافسية (v0.2)","يحتاج إلى مكون خريطة المناظر الطبيعية ومشاركات CFD","محدد لدمج تدفق العمل HORIZON"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"292a8c58401eb6d55377e078f09c6b4ed566160d11eca22f1faff5cabba393b0","qualityScore":59}');
