 الشركات الكبرى الأربع","9 شركاء من مجالات الممارسة ذات المهارات الخاصة بالمتخصصين","توفير نتائج عالية الجودة","نظام استشاري قائم على الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع إطار العمل للوكلاء والمهارات من Claude Code"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","场景规划","Claude Code","大四公司","董事会议室质量","如何使用AI智能代理","什么是场景规划","AI智能代理安装","AI智能代理设置指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","シナリオプランニング","Claude Code","ビッグ4","取締役会レベルの成果","AIエージェントの使用方法","シナリオプランニングとは","AIエージェントのインストール","AIエージェントの設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","시나리오 계획","Claude Code","빅4","이사회 수준의 결과","AI 에이전트 사용 방법","시나리오 계획이란","AI 에이전트 설치","AI 에이전트 설정 가이드"],"es":["cómo utilizar herramientas de planificación de escenarios","qué es la planificación de escenarios","Agentes de IA para la planificación de escenarios","alternativas a las grandes firmas de consultoría"," Claude Code vs otros frameworks de IA","guía de instalación de herramientas de planificación de escenarios","configuración de Agentes de IA para la planificación de escenarios"],"fr":["comment utiliser des outils de planification de scénarios","qu''est-ce que la planification de scénarios","Agents IA pour la planification de scénarios","alternatives aux grandes sociétés de conseil"," Claude Code vs d''autres frameworks IA","guide d''installation d''outils de planification de scénarios","configuration d''Agents IA pour la planification de scénarios"],"de":["wie man Szenario-Planungstools verwendet","was ist Szenario-Planung","KI-Agents für die Szenario-Planung","Alternativen zu großen Beratungsunternehmen"," Claude Code vs andere KI-Frameworks","Anleitung zur Installation von Szenario-Planungstools","Konfiguration von KI-Agents für die Szenario-Planung"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","planejamento de cenários","como usar ia para desenvolvimento","o que é ia","claude code alternative","ia vs machine learning","instalar claude code","guia de configuração da claude code"],"ru":["ИИ агенты","планирование сценариев","как использовать ИИ для разработки","что такое ИИ","альтернатива claude code","ИИ vs машинное обучение","установка claude code","руководство по настройке claude code"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تخطيط السيناريوهات","كيفية استخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي للتنمية","ما هو الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل claude code","الذكاء الاصطناعي مقابل التعلم الآلي","تثبيت claude code","دليل إعداد claude code"]}},"owner":"Kaakati","repo":"managing-director","repoPath":"Kaakati/managing-director","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T21:28:29Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Scenario Planning","description":">","bodyPreview":"# Scenario Planning & Sensitivity Analysis\n\nBuild rigorous base/bull/bear scenarios with probability-weighted expected values, trigger identification, financial impact quantification, and strategic response planning per scenario.\n\n---\n\n## Required Inputs\n\n| Input | Description | Required? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Business/project description | What is being modeled | Yes |\n| Key decision | The strategic decision these scenarios inform | Yes |\n| Time horizon | Projection period (e.g., 1-year, 3-year, 5-","body":"# Scenario Planning & Sensitivity Analysis\n\nBuild rigorous base/bull/bear scenarios with probability-weighted expected values, trigger identification, financial impact quantification, and strategic response planning per scenario.\n\n---\n\n## Required Inputs\n\n| Input | Description | Required? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Business/project description | What is being modeled | Yes |\n| Key decision | The strategic decision these scenarios inform | Yes |\n| Time horizon | Projection period (e.g., 1-year, 3-year, 5-year) | Yes |\n| Key variables | Revenue drivers, cost drivers, market factors | Yes |\n| Base case assumptions | Current best estimates | Yes |\n| Historical data | Past performance data for calibration | Recommended |\n| Industry benchmarks | Peer/industry performance ranges | Recommended |\n| Risk factors | Known threats and uncertainties | Recommended |\n| Financial model | Existing P&L, cash flow, or valuation model | If available |\n\n---\n\n## Execution Steps\n\n### Step 1: Identify Key Variables\n\nDetermine the 5-8 variables that most influence outcomes:\n\n1. **Revenue drivers**: Market size, market share, pricing, volume, win rate, churn\n2. **Cost drivers**: COGS, headcount, CAC, variable costs, CapEx\n3. **Market factors**: Growth rate, competitive intensity, regulatory changes\n4. **Operational factors**: Capacity, efficiency, time-to-market\n5. **External factors**: Macroeconomic conditions, FX rates, commodity prices\n\n**Variable prioritization matrix**:\n\n| Variable | Impact on Outcome (1-5) | Uncertainty Level (1-5) | Impact × Uncertainty | Include in Scenarios? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Variable 1] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Yes/No] |\n| [Variable 2] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Yes/No] |\n| [Variable 3] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Yes/No] |\n| [Variable 4] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Yes/No] |\n| [Variable 5] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Yes/No] |\n| [Variable 6] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Yes/No] |\n\n**Rule**: Include variables scoring >=12 on Impact x Uncertainty. Typically 4-6 variables drive 80%+ of outcome variance.\n\n### Step 2: Define Scenario Framework\n\nBuild three core scenarios plus optional stress test:\n\n| Scenario | Definition | Probability Guidance |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Bull case** | Favorable conditions across key variables; things go right | 15-25% probability |\n| **Base case** | Most likely outcome; balanced assumptions | 40-60% probability |\n| **Bear case** | Unfavorable conditions; key risks materialize | 15-25% probability |\n| **Stress test** (optional) | Extreme downside; multiple risks compound | 5-10% probability |\n\n**Probability constraint**: All scenario probabilities must sum to 100%.\n\n**Scenario construction rules**:\n1. Each scenario must be internally consistent (a world where all assumptions fit together)\n2. Scenarios should differ on the KEY drivers, not every variable\n3. Bear case is not \"everything goes wrong\" — it is the most likely bad outcome\n4. Bull case is not \"fantasy\" — it is the most likely good outcome\n5. Base case is the median expectation, not the optimistic plan relabeled\n\n### Step 3: Build Scenario Assumptions\n\nFor each key variable, define the value under each scenario:\n\n| Variable | Unit | Bear Case | Base Case | Bull Case | Stress Test |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Market growth] | % | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% |\n| [Market share] | % | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% |\n| [Average price] | $ | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| [Volume/units] | # | [X] | [X] | [X] | [X] |\n| [Churn rate] | % | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% |\n| [Gross margin] | % | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% |\n| [CAC] | $ | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| [Headcount] | # | [X] | [X] | [X] | [X] |\n\n**Calibration check**: Are the ranges supported by historical data, industry benchmarks, or analogues? If bear case has never happened in the industry''s history, it may be too extreme (or not extreme enough if tail risks are real).\n\n### Step 4: Financial Impact Quantification\n\nBuild the P&L (or relevant financial model) for each scenario:\n\n| Financial Metric | Bear Case | Base Case | Bull Case | Stress Test |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Revenue** | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| Revenue growth YoY | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% |\n| **Gross profit** | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| Gross margin | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% |\n| **Operating expenses** | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| **EBITDA** | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| EBITDA margin | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% | [X]% |\n| **Free cash flow** | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| **Cash runway** (if pre-profit) | [X] months | [X] months | [X] months | [X] months |\n\n**Multi-year projection** (repeat for each year of time horizon):\n\n| Year | Bear Revenue | Base Revenue | Bull Revenue | Bear EBITDA | Base EBITDA | Bull EBITDA |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Year 1 | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| Year 2 | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| Year 3 | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n\n### Step 5: Probability-Weighted Expected Value\n\nCalculate the expected value across scenarios:\n\n| Scenario | Probability | Revenue | EBITDA | Prob-Weighted Revenue | Prob-Weighted EBITDA |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Bull | [X]% | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| Base | [X]% | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| Bear | [X]% | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| Stress | [X]% | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| **Expected Value** | **100%** | | | **$[X]** | **$[X]** |\n\n**Key insight**: How does the expected value compare to the base case? If expected value is significantly below base case, the risk profile is skewed to the downside.\n\n### Step 6: Trigger Identification\n\nFor each scenario, identify what would cause it to materialize:\n\n| Scenario | Trigger Event | Leading Indicator | Detection Signal | Timeline |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bull** | [Event that causes upside] | [Metric to watch] | [Specific threshold] | [When visible] |\n| **Bull** | [Second trigger] | [Metric] | [Threshold] | [Timeline] |\n| **Bear** | [Event that causes downside] | [Metric to watch] | [Specific threshold] | [When visible] |\n| **Bear** | [Second trigger] | [Metric] | [Threshold] | [Timeline] |\n| **Stress** | [Extreme event] | [Metric to watch] | [Specific threshold] | [When visible] |\n\n**Monitoring cadence**: [Weekly/Monthly/Quarterly] review of leading indicators against trigger thresholds.\n\n### Step 7: Scenario Tree (Decision Mapping)\n\nMap key decision points and branching outcomes:\n\n```\n                            [Initial Decision]\n                           /         |         \\\n                    [Path A]     [Path B]     [Path C]\n                    /    \\        /    \\        /    \\\n              [Bull]  [Bear]  [Bull]  [Bear]  [Bull]  [Bear]\n              p=[X]%  p=[X]%  p=[X]%  p=[X]%  p=[X]%  p=[X]%\n              EV=$X   EV=$X   EV=$X   EV=$X   EV=$X   EV=$X\n```\n\n**Decision rule**: Choose the path with the highest expected value, subject to:\n- Acceptable downside (bear case is survivable)\n- Acceptable regret (if bull case materializes on unchosen path)\n- Strategic optionality (path preserves future flexibility)\n\n### Step 8: Monte Carlo Considerations\n\nFor key variables with continuous distributions, consider Monte Carlo simulation:\n\n1. **Define probability distributions** for each key variable:\n   - Normal: For variables with symmetric uncertainty (e.g., market growth)\n   - Log-normal: For variables that are bounded at zero (e.g., revenue)\n   - Triangular: When you know min, most likely, and max\n   - Uniform: When all values in a range are equally likely\n\n2. **Correlation matrix**: Identify which variables move together (e.g., market growth and pricing power are often correlated)\n\n3. **Simulation outputs** (if running Monte Carlo):\n   - Mean and median outcome\n   - Standard deviation\n   - 10th percentile (downside) and 90th percentile (upside)\n   - Probability of achieving target (e.g., P(revenue > $X) = Y%)\n   - Value at Risk (VaR): What is the worst outcome at 95% confidence?\n\n4. **Simplified distribution table** (when full Monte Carlo is not feasible):\n\n   | Outcome Metric | P10 (Downside) | P25 | P50 (Median) | P75 | P90 (Upside) |\n   |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   | Revenue | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n   | EBITDA | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n   | Cash flow | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n\n### Step 9: Strategic Response per Scenario\n\nDefine what actions to take under each scenario:\n\n| Scenario | Strategic Response | Resource Reallocation | Trigger to Activate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bull** | [Accelerate: increase investment, hire faster, expand] | [Where to deploy resources] | [Signal that bull case is materializing] |\n| **Base** | [Execute: stay the course, optimize] | [Standard plan] | [Default operating mode] |\n| **Bear** | [Defend: cut costs, focus on core, conserve cash] | [Where to reduce] | [Signal that bear case is materializing] |\n| **Stress** | [Survive: emergency measures, pivot consideration] | [Dramatic restructuring] | [Signal that stress case is materializing] |\n\n**Pre-committed actions**: For each scenario, define 2-3 actions that are pre-approved and can be executed immediately when triggers are hit, without additional deliberation.\n\n---\n\n## Output Template\n\n### Scenario Analysis: [Business/Project] — [Decision Context]\n\n**Date**: [Date] | **Prepared for**: [Client/Project] | **Time Horizon**: [X] years\n\n#### 1. Key Variables & Ranges\n\n| Variable | Bear | Base | Bull | Primary Data Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Var 1] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Source] |\n| [Var 2] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Source] |\n| [Var 3] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Source] |\n| [Var 4] | [X] | [X] | [X] | [Source] |\n\n#### 2. Scenario Narratives\n\n**Bull case ([X]% probability)**: [2-3 sentence narrative of what this world looks like]\n\n**Base case ([X]% probability)**: [2-3 sentence narrative]\n\n**Bear case ([X]% probability)**: [2-3 sentence narrative]\n\n**Stress test ([X]% probability)**: [2-3 sentence narrative]\n\n#### 3. Financial Impact Summary\n\n*(Include tables from Steps 4 and 5)*\n\n#### 4. Probability-Weighted Expected Value\n\n*(Include table from Step 5)*\n\n#### 5. Sensitivity Tornado\n\n| Variable | -20% Impact on EBITDA | +20% Impact on EBITDA | Range |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Var 1 — highest impact] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| [Var 2] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| [Var 3] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n| [Var 4 — lowest impact] | $[X] | $[X] | $[X] |\n\n#### 6. Trigger Dashboard\n\n*(Include table from Step 6)*\n\n#### 7. Strategic Response Plan\n\n*(Include table from Step 9)*\n\n#### 8. Decision Recommendation\n\n**Recommended path**: [Decision recommendation]\n**Expected value**: $[X]\n**Key risk**: [Primary risk with mitigation]\n**Decision reversibility**: [Reversible / Partially reversible / Irreversible]\n\n---\n\n## Quality Checks\n\n- [ ] All scenario probabilities sum to exactly 100%\n- [ ] Variable ranges are calibrated against historical data or industry benchmarks\n- [ ] Each scenario tells a coherent, internally consistent narrative (not random variable combinations)\n- [ ] Bear case is genuinely unfavorable, not just \"slightly below base case\"\n- [ ] Financial impact is quantified in dollar terms, not just directional\n- [ ] Probability-weighted expected value is calculated and compared to base case\n- [ ] Triggers are specific, measurable, and time-bound (not vague)\n- [ ] Leading indicators are identified for each trigger with monitoring cadence\n- [ ] Strategic response for each scenario includes specific pre-committed actions\n- [ ] Sensitivity tornado ranks variables by actual impact magnitude\n- [ ] Stress test addresses existential risk (can the business survive?)\n- [ ] Decision recommendation addresses reversibility and optionality\n- [ ] Monte Carlo considerations address variable correlations, not just independent ranges\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T04:03:50.648Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Strategic Planning Agents requiring advanced probability-weighted scenario analysis and financial impact quantification.","zh":"适用于需要高级概率加权场景分析和财务影响量化的战略规划代理","ja":"高度な確率重み付きシナリオ分析と財務的影響量化を必要とする戦略的計画エージェントに最適","ko":"고급 확률 가중 시나리오 분석 및 재무 영향량을 필요로 하는 전략적 계획 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de planificación estratégica que requieren un análisis de escenarios con ponderación de probabilidad avanzada y cuantificación del impacto financiero.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de planification stratégique nécessitant une analyse de scénarios à pondération de probabilité avancée et une quantification de l''impact financier.","de":"Ideal für strategische Planungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Wahrscheinlichkeits-gewichtete Szenarioanalyse und eine finanzielle Auswirkungsquantifizierung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Planejamento Estratégico que exigem análise de cenário avançada com peso de probabilidade e quantificação de impacto financeiro.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Стратегических Планировочных Агентов, требующих расширенного анализа сценариев с весом вероятности и количественной оценки финансового воздействия.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التخطيط الاستراتيجي الذين يتطلبون تحليل سيناريو متقدم مع وزن الإحتمال وتقدير التأثير المالي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build rigorous base/bull/bear scenarios with trigger identification, financial impact quantification, and strategic response planning using probability-weighted expected values, facilitating informed decision-making through sensitivity analysis and scenario planning protocols.","zh":"赋予代理构建严格的基础/看涨/看跌场景，包括触发点识别、财务影响量化和战略响应规划，使用概率加权预期值，促进通过敏感性分析和场景规划协议的明智决策","ja":"エージェントは、トリガー識別、財務的影響量化、戦略的対応計画を使用して、厳格なベース/ブル/ベアシナリオを構築し、確率重み付き期待値によって、感覚分析およびシナリオ計画プロトコルを通じて情報に基づいた意思決定を促進する","ko":"에이전트가 엄격한 기본/불/불 시나리오를 구축할 수 있도록 하여 트리거 식별, 재무적 영향량, 전략적 대응 계획을 사용하고, 확률 가중 기대값을 통해 민감성 분석 및 시나리오 계획 프로토콜을 통해 정보에 의거한 의사결정을 촉진","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir escenarios base/toro/oso rigurosos con identificación de desencadenantes, cuantificación del impacto financiero y planificación de respuestas estratégicas utilizando valores esperados con ponderación de probabilidad, facilitando la toma de decisiones informadas a través de análisis de sensibilidad y protocolos de planificación de escenarios.","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des scénarios base/bull/bear rigoureux avec identification de déclencheurs, quantification de l''impact financier et planification de réponses stratégiques en utilisant des valeurs attendues à pondération de probabilité, facilitant la prise de décisions éclairées à travers l''analyse de sensibilité et les protocoles de planification de scénarios.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, strenge Basis-/Bullen-/Bären-Szenarien mit Triggeridentifizierung, finanzieller Auswirkungsquantifizierung und strategischer Reaktionsplanung unter Verwendung von wahrscheinlichkeitsgewichteten Erwartungswerten zu erstellen, um durch Sensitivitätsanalyse und Szenarioplanungsprotokolle fundierte Entscheidungen zu ermöglichen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes construam cenários rigorosos base/bull/bear com identificação de gatilhos, quantificação de impacto financeiro e planejamento de resposta estratégica usando valores esperados com peso de probabilidade, facilitando a tomada de decisões informadas por meio de análise de sensibilidade e protocolos de planejamento de cenários.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать строгие базовые/буль/bear-сценарии с идентификацией триггеров, количественной оценкой финансового воздействия и стратегическим планированием ответа с использованием вероятностно-взвешенных ожидаемых значений, что облегчает принятие обоснованных решений посредством анализа чувствительности и протоколов планирования сценариев.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من بناء سيناريوهات قوية قاعدة/دب/دببة مع تحديد المحددات وتقدير التأثير المالي وتخطيط الاستجابة الاستراتيجية باستخدام القيم المتوقعة الموزونة بالاحتمال، مما يسهل اتخاذ القرارات المستنيرة من خلال تحليل الحساسية وبروتوكولات تخطيط السيناريوهات."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating scenario planning for business projects with multiple stakeholders","Generating financial models with probability-weighted expected values for investment decisions","Debugging strategic response plans to mitigate potential risks and maximize opportunities"],"zh":["自动化具有多个利益相关者的商业项目场景规划","生成具有概率加权预期值的财务模型以进行投资决策","调试战略响应计划以减轻潜在风险并最大化机会"],"ja":["複数の利害関係者を持つビジネスプロジェクトのシナリオ計画を自動化する","投資決定のための確率重み付き期待値を持つ財務モデルを生成する","潜在的なリスクを軽減し、機会を最大化するための戦略的対応計画のデバッグ"],"ko":["여러 이해관계자를 가진 비즈니스 프로젝트의 시나리오 계획을 자동화하는 것","투자 결정에 대한 확률 가중 기대값을 가진 재무 모델을 생성하는 것","潜在적인 위험을 경감시키고 기회를 최대화하기 위한 전략적 대응 계획의 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de la planificación de escenarios para proyectos empresariales con múltiples partes interesadas","Generación de modelos financieros con valores esperados con ponderación de probabilidad para decisiones de inversión","Depuración de planes de respuesta estratégica para mitigar riesgos potenciales y maximizar oportunidades"],"fr":["Automatisation de la planification de scénarios pour les projets d''entreprise avec plusieurs parties prenantes","Génération de modèles financiers avec des valeurs attendues à pondération de probabilité pour les décisions d''investissement","Débogage des plans de réponse stratégique pour atténuer les risques potentiels et maximiser les opportunités"],"de":["Automatisierung der Szenarioplanung für Geschäftsprojekte mit mehreren Beteiligten","Erstellung von Finanzmodellen mit wahrscheinlichkeitsgewichteten Erwartungswerten für Investitionsentscheidungen","Fehlerbehebung bei strategischen Reaktionsplänen, um potenzielle Risiken zu mindern und Chancen zu maximieren"],"pt":["Automatizar o planejamento de cenários para projetos de negócios com vários stakeholders","Gerar modelos financeiros com valores esperados com peso de probabilidade para decisões de investimento","Depurar planos de resposta estratégica para mitigar riscos potenciais e maximizar oportunidades"],"ru":["Автоматизация планирования сценариев для бизнес-проектов с несколькими заинтересованными сторонами","Генерация финансовых моделей с вероятностно-взвешенными ожидаемыми значениями для инвестиционных решений","Отладка стратегических планов ответа для смягчения потенциальных рисков и максимизации возможностей"],"ar":["تأتمتة تخطيط السيناريوهات لمشاريع الأعمال مع عدد من أصحاب المصلحة","генерация نماذج مالية مع قيم متوقعة موزونة بالاحتمال لقرارات الاستثمار","تصحيح أخطاء خطط الاستجابة الاستراتيجية لتخفيف المخاطر المحتملة وتحقيق الفرص القصوى"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires business/project description and key decision inputs","Needs specific time horizon for projection period","Limited to financial impact quantification and strategic response planning"],"zh":["需要商业/项目描述和关键决策输入","需要特定的时间范围用于预测期","仅限于财务影响量化和战略响应规划"],"ja":["ビジネス/プロジェクトの説明と重要な意思決定入力を必要とする","プロジェクション期間の特定の時間範囲を必要とする","財務的影響量化と戦略的対応計画に限定される"],"ko":["비즈니스/프로젝트 설명 및 주요 의사결정 입력이 필요","예측 기간을 위한 특정 시간 범위가 필요","재무적 영향량 및 전략적 대응 계획에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere descripción del negocio/proyecto y entradas de decisión clave","Necesita un horizonte de tiempo específico para el período de proyección","Limitado a la cuantificación del impacto financiero y la planificación de respuestas estratégicas"],"fr":["Nécessite une description de l''entreprise/projet et des entrées de décision clés","A besoin d''un horizon de temps spécifique pour la période de projection","Limité à la quantification de l''impact financier et à la planification de réponses stratégiques"],"de":["Benötigt eine Beschreibung des Geschäfts/Projekts und wichtige Entscheidungseingaben","Benötigt einen bestimmten Zeitrahmen für den Prognosezeitraum","Begrenzt auf die Quantifizierung der finanziellen Auswirkungen und die strategische Reaktionsplanung"],"pt":["Exige descrição do negócio/projeto e entradas de decisão-chave","Necessita de um horizonte de tempo específico para o período de projeção","Limitado à quantificação de impacto financeiro e planejamento de resposta estratégica"],"ru":["Требует описания бизнеса/проекта и ключевых входных данных для принятия решений","Требует конкретного временного горизонта для периода прогнозирования","Ограничен количественной оценкой финансового воздействия и стратегическим планированием ответа"],"ar":["يتطلب وصف الأعمال/المشروع ومعلومات القرار الرئيسية","يحتاج إلى أفق زمني محدد للفترة المقدرة","محدود بتقييم التأثير المالي وتخطيط الاستجابة الاستراتيجية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"bc8ffbeeb800654c8b4dc0ce0a3a8e4cd807580808c64a38a93f8134481885e2","qualityScore":57}');
